  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The perimeter of a semicircular region, measured in centimeters, is numerically equal to its area, measured in square centimeters. The radius of the semicircle, measured in centimeters, is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\pi\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\frac2\\pi\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\frac12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\frac4\\pi+2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1982-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For \\(r\\gt0,\\) equality of perimeter and area gives \\(\\pi r+2r=\\frac{\\pi r^2}{2}.\\) Dividing by \\(r\\) and solving yields \\(r=\\frac{2(\\pi+2)}{\\pi}=2+\\frac{4}{\\pi}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Include the diameter in the perimeter of the region",
        "Set \\(\\pi r+2r\\) equal to \\(\\frac{\\pi r^2}{2}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
